IMPORT prelude

-- Copyright Act 1968 (Commonwealth) -- who owns the code I write at work, is software a literary work, how long does the
-- copyright last, what may only the owner do, how is it assigned, and what moral rights do I keep?
--
-- SEAT: the employee-author and the founder -- the person who writes the code, whether as an employee, a contractor, or a
-- founder-director, and who asks "Who owns the code I write at work?". Every decision is phrased as that person asks it,
-- from facts they could state. The founder asks the same questions from the other side ("does my company own what my
-- engineer wrote, and what I wrote myself?"); the answers come from the same rules.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 10(1) ("computer program", "literary work", "work"), s 22(1) (when a work is made), s 29A (made
-- public), s 31 (the exclusive rights in a work), s 32 (works in which copyright subsists; "qualified person", s 32(4)),
-- s 33(2), (3) (duration), s 35 (ownership: the author; periodical employees, s 35(4); commissioned photographs, portraits and
-- engravings, s 35(5); employees under a contract of service, s 35(6); agreements to the contrary, s 35(3)), s 36(1)
-- (infringement), s 47B(1), (2) (the copy made in running a program), s 80 (joint authors: the last to die), s 196(1)-(3)
-- (assignment in writing signed by the assignor), s 197(1) (assignment of future copyright), Part IX: ss 189, 190, 192, 193,
-- 194(1), 195AC, 195AI (the author's moral rights), s 195AM(2), (3) (their duration), s 195AN (who exercises them; not
-- transmissible), s 195AO (infringing attribution), s 195AR(1) (reasonable not to identify), s 195AWA (the author's written
-- consent; an employee's blanket consent, s 195AWA(4)), s 195AWB (consent invalidated), s 195AX (acts outside Australia).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 65, compilation date 2 April 2026 ("Includes amendments: Act No. 29, 2026"; register id
-- C2026C00138), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1968A00063.txt (retrieved 2026-10-13). No regulations used:
-- the plan names none, and whether regulations under s 184 extend the Act to a foreign work is an INPUT.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: subject-matter other than works (Part IV: sound recordings, films, broadcasts, published editions) except to
-- say they are not "works"; the other exceptions to infringement (fair dealing, ss 40-43; s 47C back-up copies and the rest of
-- Part III Division 4A); s 47AB's wider "computer program" for Division 4A; commercial rental before 1994 (s 31(6), (7));
-- remedies, damages and offences (Part V); Crown copyright (Part VII) and the prescribed-organisation provisions (Part X) to
-- which s 35 is subject; pseudonymous joint works (s 81); the moral rights of performers and of film makers, and consent for
-- films (s 195AW); derogatory treatment (ss 195AJ-195AL) beyond the word; the tribunal, collecting societies and statutory
-- licences. Whether a program is "original", whether someone is an employee under a "contract of service", and whether the
-- work was made "in pursuance of the terms of" the employment are borrowed from the general law and asked as FACTS. Patents
-- and trade marks (the same life event) are other Acts.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the individual's seat with the design defaults ruled on
-- 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use as advice. Years
-- are calendar years written as numbers. Judgments the Act hands to a court are INPUTS ("if it was reasonable in all the
-- circumstances not to identify me").

§ `Copyright Act 1968`

§§ `10(1) -- is my code a literary work`

-- s 10(1): "computer program means a set of statements or instructions to be used directly or indirectly in a computer in
-- order to bring about a certain result."
@export Is what I wrote a computer program (s 10(1))?
GIVEN `it is a set of statements or instructions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what you wrote is a set of statements or instructions (source code, object code, scripts)
      `it is to be used directly or indirectly in a computer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is meant to be used in a computer, directly or through compilation or interpretation
      `it is to bring about a certain result` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is meant to make the computer bring about a certain result
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I wrote a computer program` IF
        `it is a set of statements or instructions`
    AND `it is to be used directly or indirectly in a computer`
    AND `it is to bring about a certain result`

-- s 10(1): "literary work includes: (a) a table, or compilation, expressed in words, figures or symbols; and (b) a computer
-- program or compilation of computer programs." "work means a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic work."
-- "Includes": other writing is a literary work in its ordinary sense, which is borrowed and asked as a fact (the kind).
DECLARE `Kind of material` IS ONE OF
    `a computer program or a compilation of computer programs`
    `a table or compilation expressed in words, figures or symbols`
    `other writing that is a literary work in the ordinary sense`
    `a dramatic work`
    `a musical work`
    `an artistic work`
    `a sound recording or a cinematograph film`

@export Is it a literary work (s 10(1))?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of material` @desc What kind of thing it is
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a literary work` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a computer program or a compilation of computer programs` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a table or compilation expressed in words, figures or symbols` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `other writing that is a literary work in the ordinary sense` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@export Is it a "work" in the Act's sense -- literary, dramatic, musical or artistic (s 10(1))?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of material` @desc What kind of thing it is
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it a work` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a sound recording or a cinematograph film` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of material`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `literary, dramatic or artistic` IF
    `Is it a literary work` `the kind`
    OR (CONSIDER `the kind`
        WHEN `a dramatic work` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an artistic work` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE)

§§ `22(1), 32 -- does copyright subsist in my work`

-- s 22(1): a work is made "when ... the work was first reduced to writing or to some other material form". s 10(1):
-- "material form ... includes any form (whether visible or not) of storage of the work" -- code saved to disk is in material
-- form.
-- s 32(1): "copyright subsists in an original literary, dramatic, musical or artistic work that is unpublished and of which the
-- author: (a) was a qualified person at the time when the work was made; or (b) if the making of the work extended over a
-- period--was a qualified person for a substantial part of that period."
-- s 32(2): where the work "has been published ... copyright subsists in the work ... if, but only if: (c) the first
-- publication of the work took place in Australia; (d) the author of the work was a qualified person at the time when the
-- work was first published; or (e) the author died before that time but was a qualified person immediately before his or her
-- death." s 32(4): "qualified person means an Australian citizen or a person resident in Australia."
-- "Original" is not defined: asked as a fact. Regulations under s 184 may apply the Act to works and people of other
-- countries; none are deposited, so their effect is an INPUT.
DECLARE `My work` HAS
    `the kind` IS A `Kind of material`
    @desc What kind of thing it is
    `it is original` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it is original (it originates with its author and is not copied)
    `it has been reduced to writing or another material form` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it has been written down or stored in any form, visible or not (a file on disk counts)
    `it has been published` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it has been published
    `it was first published in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether its first publication took place in Australia
    `the author was a citizen or resident of Australia when it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the author was an Australian citizen or resident when it was made (or for a substantial part of the making)
    `the author was a citizen or resident of Australia when it was first published` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the author was an Australian citizen or resident at first publication
    `the author died before publication, a citizen or resident of Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the author died before first publication and was an Australian citizen or resident immediately before death
    `regulations under section 184 extend the Act to it` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether regulations under s 184 apply the Act to this work because of a foreign country, citizenship or residence

@export Does copyright subsist in my work (ss 22(1), 32)?
GIVEN `the work` IS A `My work` @desc The facts about your work
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does copyright subsist in my work` IF
        `Is it a work` (`the work`'s `the kind`)
    AND `the work`'s `it is original`
    AND `the work`'s `it has been reduced to writing or another material form`
    AND (   `the work`'s `regulations under section 184 extend the Act to it`
         OR (    (NOT `the work`'s `it has been published`)
             AND `the work`'s `the author was a citizen or resident of Australia when it was made`)
         OR (    `the work`'s `it has been published`
             AND (   `the work`'s `it was first published in Australia`
                  OR `the work`'s `the author was a citizen or resident of Australia when it was first published`
                  OR `the work`'s `the author died before publication, a citizen or resident of Australia`)))

§§ `35 -- who first owns the copyright in what I made`

-- s 35(2): "Subject to this section, the author of a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic work is the owner of any
-- copyright subsisting in the work by virtue of this Part."
-- s 35(3): "The operation of any of the next three succeeding subsections in relation to copyright in a particular work may be
-- excluded or modified by agreement." (The text asks for an "agreement"; unlike s 196(3) it does not ask for writing.)
-- s 35(4): a literary, dramatic or artistic work "made by the author under the terms of his or her employment by the
-- proprietor of a newspaper, magazine or similar periodical under a contract of service or apprenticeship; and ... so made for
-- the purpose of inclusion in a newspaper, magazine or similar periodical": the author owns only the book and hard-copy
-- facsimile rights in (c); "(d) except as provided by paragraph (c), the proprietor is the owner of the copyright."
-- s 35(5): where "a person makes, for valuable consideration, an agreement with another person for the taking of a photograph
-- for a private or domestic purpose, the painting or drawing of a portrait or the making of an engraving by the other person;
-- and ... the work is made in pursuance of the agreement; the first-mentioned person is the owner".
-- s 35(6): "Where a literary, dramatic or artistic work to which neither of the last two preceding subsections applies, or a
-- musical work, is made by the author in pursuance of the terms of his or her employment by another person under a contract
-- of service or apprenticeship, that other person is the owner of any copyright subsisting in the work by virtue of this Part."
-- So commissioned software (a contract FOR services) stays with its author: s 35(5) reaches only photographs, portraits and
-- engravings. Only a total exclusion of s 35(4)-(6) is encoded; a modification "by agreement" is too open to model.
DECLARE `Owner` IS ONE OF
    `the author`
    `the author's employer`
    `the person who commissioned it`
    `the periodical proprietor, except the author's book and facsimile rights`
    `nobody, because no copyright subsists`

DECLARE `How it was made` HAS
    `I made it under a contract of service or apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you made it as an employee (or apprentice) under a contract of service, not as a contractor or a director without an employment contract
    `I made it in pursuance of the terms of that employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether making it was part of what your employment required of you (not a side project outside your duties)
    `my employer publishes a newspaper, magazine or similar periodical` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether your employer is the proprietor of a newspaper, magazine or similar periodical
    `I made it for inclusion in a newspaper, magazine or similar periodical` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it was made to be included in a newspaper, magazine or similar periodical
    `someone paid me under an agreement to make it` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether someone made an agreement with you, for valuable consideration, for you to make it
    `it is a private photograph, a portrait or an engraving` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it is a photograph for a private or domestic purpose, a painted or drawn portrait, or an engraving
    `an agreement keeps the copyright with me` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether an agreement with the employer or commissioner excludes their statutory ownership, leaving the copyright with you

@export Who first owns the copyright in what I made (s 35)?
GIVEN `the work` IS A `My work` @desc The facts about the work
      `how` IS A `How it was made` @desc The circumstances in which you made it
GIVETH AN `Owner`
DECIDE `Who first owns the copyright in what I made` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `Does copyright subsist in my work` `the work`
            THEN `nobody, because no copyright subsists`
        IF `how`'s `an agreement keeps the copyright with me`
            THEN `the author`
        IF `s 35(4): a periodical employee's work` `the work` `how`
            THEN `the periodical proprietor, except the author's book and facsimile rights`
        IF `s 35(5): a commissioned photograph, portrait or engraving` `the work` `how`
            THEN `the person who commissioned it`
        IF `s 35(6): an employee's work` `the work` `how`
            THEN `the author's employer`
        OTHERWISE `the author`

GIVEN `how` IS A `How it was made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `made under a contract of service, in pursuance of its terms` IF
        `how`'s `I made it under a contract of service or apprenticeship`
    AND `how`'s `I made it in pursuance of the terms of that employment`

GIVEN `the work` IS A `My work`
      `how` IS A `How it was made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35(4): a periodical employee's work` IF
        `literary, dramatic or artistic` (`the work`'s `the kind`)
    AND `made under a contract of service, in pursuance of its terms` `how`
    AND `how`'s `my employer publishes a newspaper, magazine or similar periodical`
    AND `how`'s `I made it for inclusion in a newspaper, magazine or similar periodical`

GIVEN `the work` IS A `My work`
      `how` IS A `How it was made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35(5): a commissioned photograph, portrait or engraving` IF
        `the work`'s `the kind` EQUALS `an artistic work`
    AND `how`'s `someone paid me under an agreement to make it`
    AND `how`'s `it is a private photograph, a portrait or an engraving`

GIVEN `the work` IS A `My work`
      `how` IS A `How it was made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 35(6): an employee's work` IF
        `Is it a work` (`the work`'s `the kind`)
    AND `made under a contract of service, in pursuance of its terms` `how`

§§ `196, 197 -- assigning the copyright`

-- s 196(1): "Copyright is personal property and, subject to this section, is transmissible by assignment, by will and by
-- devolution by operation of law." (2): "An assignment of copyright may be limited in any way, including ... (a) ... one or
-- more of the classes of acts ...; (b) ... a place in or part of Australia; (c) ... part of the period for which the copyright
-- is to subsist." (3): "An assignment of copyright (whether total or partial) does not have effect unless it is in writing
-- signed by or on behalf of the assignor."
-- s 197(1): where "by an agreement made in relation to a future copyright and signed by or on behalf of the person who would
-- ... be the owner of the copyright on its coming into existence, that person purports to assign the future copyright ...
-- the copyright, on its coming into existence, vests in the assignee". The further condition (that the assignee would be
-- "entitled as against all other persons to have the copyright vested") is a question of the general law, read here as met
-- by the signed agreement (an INFERENCE). A signed agreement is read as a written one.
DECLARE `Assignment` HAS
    `there is an assignment` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the owner (or the person who will own it) has assigned, or agreed to assign, the copyright
    `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the assignment is in writing
    `it is signed by or for the assignor` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it is signed by the person assigning, or on their behalf
    `it is limited to some acts, places or part of the term` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it assigns only some of the exclusive rights, only some places, or only part of the period

@export Does the assignment pass the copyright, or the future copyright (ss 196(3), 197(1))?
GIVEN `the assignment` IS AN `Assignment` @desc The facts about the assignment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the assignment pass the copyright` IF
        `the assignment`'s `there is an assignment`
    AND `the assignment`'s `it is in writing`
    AND `the assignment`'s `it is signed by or for the assignor`

DECLARE `Holder` IS ONE OF
    `the first owner`
    `the assignee`
    `the assignee for what was assigned, the first owner for the rest`
    `nobody, because no copyright subsists`

@export Who owns the copyright now, after any assignment (ss 35, 196, 197)?
GIVEN `the work` IS A `My work` @desc The facts about the work
      `how` IS A `How it was made` @desc The circumstances in which it was made
      `the assignment` IS AN `Assignment` @desc Any assignment by the first owner
GIVETH A `Holder`
DECIDE `Who owns the copyright now` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `Does copyright subsist in my work` `the work`
            THEN `nobody, because no copyright subsists`
        IF NOT `Does the assignment pass the copyright` `the assignment`
            THEN `the first owner`
        IF `the assignment`'s `it is limited to some acts, places or part of the term`
            THEN `the assignee for what was assigned, the first owner for the rest`
        OTHERWISE `the assignee`

§§ `31 -- what only the owner may do`

-- s 31(1): copyright "is the exclusive right: (a) in the case of a literary, dramatic or musical work, to do all or any of the
-- following acts: (i) to reproduce the work in a material form; (ii) to publish the work; (iii) to perform the work in public;
-- (iv) to communicate the work to the public; (vi) to make an adaptation of the work; (vii) to do, in relation to a work that
-- is an adaptation of the first-mentioned work, any of the acts specified ... in subparagraphs (i) to (iv) ...; (b) in the
-- case of an artistic work ... (i) to reproduce ...; (ii) to publish ...; (iii) to communicate the work to the public; and
-- (c) in the case of a literary work (other than a computer program) or a musical or dramatic work, to enter into a
-- commercial rental arrangement in respect of the work reproduced in a sound recording; and (d) in the case of a computer
-- program, to enter into a commercial rental arrangement in respect of the program."
-- s 31(3): (d) does not extend to "a machine or device in which a computer program is embodied if the program is not able to
-- be copied in the course of the ordinary use of the machine or device"; s 31(5): nor "if the computer program is not the
-- essential object of the rental".
DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `reproduce it in a material form`
    `publish it`
    `perform it in public`
    `communicate it to the public`
    `make an adaptation of it`
    `reproduce, publish, perform or communicate an adaptation of it`
    `rent it out commercially`
    `an act section 31 does not list`

DECLARE `What is done` HAS
    `the act` IS AN `Act`
    @desc What is done with the work
    `the program is the essential object of the rental` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc For a rental of a program: whether the program is the essential object of the rental
    `the program is in a machine and cannot be copied in its ordinary use` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc For a rental of a program: whether it is embodied in a machine or device and cannot be copied in ordinary use
    `what is rented is a sound recording of the work` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc For a rental of another literary, dramatic or musical work: whether what is rented is the work reproduced in a sound recording
    `it is done or authorised in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it is done, or authorised, in Australia
    `it is only the automatic copy made in running a copy of the program` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the only reproduction is the one made incidentally and automatically in running a copy of the program for the purpose it was designed for
    `the copy run is owned or licensed by whoever runs it` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the copy is run by or for its owner or licensee
    `the copy run is an infringing copy` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the copy run is itself an infringing copy
    `it goes against an express direction or licence given with the copy` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether running it goes against an express direction or licence given by the copyright owner when the copy was acquired

@export Is this act one of the copyright owner's exclusive rights (s 31)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of material` @desc What kind of work it is
      `what` IS A `What is done` @desc What is done with it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this one of the owner's exclusive rights` IF
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `Is it a work` `the kind`
            THEN FALSE
        IF `the kind` EQUALS `an artistic work`
            THEN `s 31(1)(b): an artistic work's right` `what`
        OTHERWISE `s 31(1)(a), (c), (d): a literary, dramatic or musical work's right` `the kind` `what`

GIVEN `what` IS A `What is done`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 31(1)(b): an artistic work's right` IF
    CONSIDER `what`'s `the act`
    WHEN `reproduce it in a material form` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `publish it` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `communicate it to the public` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of material`
      `what` IS A `What is done`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 31(1)(a), (c), (d): a literary, dramatic or musical work's right` IF
    CONSIDER `what`'s `the act`
    WHEN `an act section 31 does not list` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `rent it out commercially` THEN `s 31(1)(c), (d): a rental the owner controls` `the kind` `what`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of material`
      `what` IS A `What is done`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 31(1)(c), (d): a rental the owner controls` IF
    IF `the kind` EQUALS `a computer program or a compilation of computer programs`
    THEN     `what`'s `the program is the essential object of the rental`
         AND (NOT `what`'s `the program is in a machine and cannot be copied in its ordinary use`)
    ELSE `what`'s `what is rented is a sound recording of the work`

§§ `36(1), 47B -- would I infringe`

-- s 36(1): "the copyright in a literary, dramatic, musical or artistic work is infringed by a person who, not being the owner
-- of the copyright, and without the licence of the owner of the copyright, does in Australia, or authorizes the doing in
-- Australia of, any act comprised in the copyright."
-- s 47B(1): not infringed by a reproduction "incidentally and automatically made as part of the technical process of running a
-- copy of the program for the purposes for which the program was designed; and ... the running of the copy is done by, or on
-- behalf of, the owner or licensee of the copy"; (2) not "from an infringing copy" nor "contrary to an express direction or
-- licence given by, or on behalf of, the owner of the copyright ... when the owner or licensee of that copy acquired it".
-- The employee who leaves and takes the employer's code is "not being the owner": copying it infringes unless licensed.
@export Would I infringe the copyright by doing this (ss 36(1), 47B)?
GIVEN `the work` IS A `My work` @desc The facts about the work
      `what` IS A `What is done` @desc What you would do with it
      `I own the copyright` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you own the copyright (or the part of it covering this act)
      `I have the owner's licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the copyright owner has licensed you to do it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Would I infringe the copyright` IF
        `Does copyright subsist in my work` `the work`
    AND (NOT `I own the copyright`)
    AND (NOT `I have the owner's licence`)
    AND `what`'s `it is done or authorised in Australia`
    AND `Is this one of the owner's exclusive rights` (`the work`'s `the kind`) `what`
    AND (NOT `the s 47B running exception applies` (`the work`'s `the kind`) `what`)

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of material`
      `what` IS A `What is done`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 47B running exception applies` IF
        `the kind` EQUALS `a computer program or a compilation of computer programs`
    AND `what`'s `the act` EQUALS `reproduce it in a material form`
    AND `what`'s `it is only the automatic copy made in running a copy of the program`
    AND `what`'s `the copy run is owned or licensed by whoever runs it`
    AND (NOT `what`'s `the copy run is an infringing copy`)
    AND (NOT `what`'s `it goes against an express direction or licence given with the copy`)

§§ `29A, 33, 80 -- how long the copyright lasts`

-- s 33(2), works "first made public before 1 January 2019": item 1, "70 years after the calendar year in which the author of
-- the work died"; item 2, where "(a) the work is: (i) a literary work (other than a computer program); or (ii) a dramatic
-- work; or (iii) a musical work; or (iv) an engraving; and (b) the author of the work has died; and (c) the work was not first
-- made public before the author died; and (d) item 3 does not apply": "70 years after the calendar year in which the work was
-- first made public"; item 3, where "the identity of the author of the work is not generally known at any time before the end
-- of 70 years after the calendar year in which the work was first made public": the same.
-- s 33(3), works "not first made public before 1 January 2019": item 1 as above; item 2, where "(a) the identity of the
-- author is not generally known at any time before the end of 70 years after the calendar year in which the work was made; and
-- (b) the work is not first made public before the end of 50 years after the calendar year in which the work was made": "70
-- years after the calendar year in which the work was made"; item 3, unknown identity and "first made public before the end of
-- 50 years after the calendar year in which the work was made": "70 years after the calendar year in which the work was first
-- made public".
-- s 80: for a "work of joint authorship", the author in item 1 (and s 33(2) item 2) is "the author who died last".
-- The copyright "continues to subsist until" 70 years after the year: read as lasting to the end of that 70th year, which is
-- the number returned (an INFERENCE about "until"). The employer's ownership does not change the term: it runs from the
-- AUTHOR's death. While the author lives (or an unknown author's work could still be made public in time) the last year is
-- not yet fixed: NOTHING. Engravings are not separated from other artistic works (not needed by the events). The two 70-year
-- windows for "not generally known" are one input.
DECLARE `Life of the work` HAS
    `the kind` IS A `Kind of material`
    @desc What kind of work it is
    `the year it was made` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The calendar year it was first written down or stored
    `it has been made public` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it has been published, performed, communicated to the public, or offered on records to the public
    `the year it was first made public` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The calendar year it was first made public (0 if never)
    `the author has died` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the author (for joint authors, the last of them) has died
    `the year the author died` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The calendar year the author (or the last joint author) died (0 if alive)
    `it was first made public before the author died` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it was first made public before the author died
    `the author's identity is generally known` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the author's identity has been generally known (not an anonymous work)
    `the current year` IS A NUMBER
    @desc The calendar year now

GIVEN `l` IS A `Life of the work`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `70 years after the author's death` IS
    IF `l`'s `the author has died` THEN JUST (`l`'s `the year the author died` PLUS 70) ELSE NOTHING

@export What is the last calendar year in which copyright in the work subsists (ss 33, 80)?
GIVEN `l` IS A `Life of the work` @desc The facts about the work's making, publication and author
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the last year the copyright lasts` IS
    IF `first made public before 1 January 2019` `l`
    THEN `s 33(2): the table for works made public before 2019` `l`
    ELSE `s 33(3): the table for other works` `l`

GIVEN `l` IS A `Life of the work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `first made public before 1 January 2019` IF
    `l`'s `it has been made public` AND `l`'s `the year it was first made public` < 2019

GIVEN `l` IS A `Life of the work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a literary (not a program), dramatic or musical work` IF
    CONSIDER `l`'s `the kind`
    WHEN `a table or compilation expressed in words, figures or symbols` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `other writing that is a literary work in the ordinary sense` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a dramatic work` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a musical work` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `l` IS A `Life of the work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 33(2) item 2 applies` IF
        `a literary (not a program), dramatic or musical work` `l`
    AND `l`'s `the author has died`
    AND (NOT `l`'s `it was first made public before the author died`)

GIVEN `l` IS A `Life of the work`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 33(2): the table for works made public before 2019` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `l`'s `the author's identity is generally known`
            THEN JUST (`l`'s `the year it was first made public` PLUS 70)
        IF `s 33(2) item 2 applies` `l`
            THEN JUST (`l`'s `the year it was first made public` PLUS 70)
        OTHERWISE `70 years after the author's death` `l`

GIVEN `l` IS A `Life of the work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `made public within 50 years of the year it was made` IF
    `l`'s `it has been made public` AND `l`'s `the year it was first made public` <= `l`'s `the year it was made` PLUS 50

-- Item 2 needs the work "not first made public before the end of 50 years after the calendar year in which the work was
-- made": known once it was made public later than that, or once that year has passed with the work unpublished.
GIVEN `l` IS A `Life of the work`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not made public within 50 years, and that is now known` IF
        (NOT `made public within 50 years of the year it was made` `l`)
    AND (`l`'s `it has been made public` OR `l`'s `the current year` > `l`'s `the year it was made` PLUS 50)

GIVEN `l` IS A `Life of the work`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 33(3): the table for other works` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `l`'s `the author's identity is generally known`
            THEN `70 years after the author's death` `l`
        IF `made public within 50 years of the year it was made` `l`
            THEN JUST (`l`'s `the year it was first made public` PLUS 70)
        IF `not made public within 50 years, and that is now known` `l`
            THEN JUST (`l`'s `the year it was made` PLUS 70)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `189, 190, 193, 195AC, 195AI -- do I have moral rights in it`

-- s 190: "Only individuals have moral rights." s 193(1): "The author of a work has a right of attribution of authorship";
-- s 195AC(1): "a right not to have authorship of the work falsely attributed"; s 195AI(1): "a right of integrity of
-- authorship". s 189: in Part IX "literary work means a literary work in which copyright subsists" (and so for dramatic,
-- musical and artistic works). s 192(1): the moral rights "are in addition to any other rights in relation to the work that
-- the author or anyone else has under this Act" -- so the employee-author keeps them though the employer owns the copyright,
-- and a company that owns the copyright has none.
@export Do I have moral rights in the work -- attribution, against false attribution, and integrity (ss 189, 190, 193, 195AC, 195AI)?
GIVEN `the work` IS A `My work` @desc The facts about the work
      `I am the author` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are the author (the person who wrote it)
      `I am an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a human being, not a company
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have moral rights in it` IF
        `I am an individual`
    AND `I am the author`
    AND `Is it a work` (`the work`'s `the kind`)
    AND `Does copyright subsist in my work` `the work`

-- s 195AM(2): integrity "in respect of a work other than a cinematograph film continues in force until copyright ceases to
-- subsist in the work"; (3): the other moral rights likewise.
@export What is the last calendar year my moral rights in the work last (s 195AM)?
GIVEN `l` IS A `Life of the work` @desc The facts about the work's making, publication and author
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the last year my moral rights last` IS `What is the last year the copyright lasts` `l`

§§ `195AN -- who may exercise my moral rights`

-- s 195AN(1): after the author dies, the moral rights "may be exercised and enforced by his or her legal personal
-- representative"; (2): "If the affairs of the author of a work are lawfully administered by another person (except under a
-- law for the relief of bankrupt or insolvent debtors), the author's moral rights may be exercised and enforced by the person
-- administering his or her affairs." (3): "a moral right in respect of a work is not transmissible by assignment, by will, or
-- by devolution by operation of law."
@export Can I assign, sell or leave by will my moral rights (s 195AN(3))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I assign or bequeath my moral rights` IS FALSE

DECLARE `Who enforces` IS ONE OF
    `I do`
    `my legal personal representative`
    `the person lawfully administering my affairs`

@export Who may exercise and enforce my moral rights (s 195AN(1), (2))?
GIVEN `I have died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the author has died
      `my affairs are lawfully administered by another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether someone else lawfully administers your affairs (for example under a guardianship or administration order)
      `that administration is under a bankruptcy or insolvency law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that administration is under a law for the relief of bankrupt or insolvent debtors
GIVETH A `Who enforces`
DECIDE `Who may enforce my moral rights` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `I have died`
            THEN `my legal personal representative`
        IF `my affairs are lawfully administered by another person` AND (NOT `that administration is under a bankruptcy or insolvency law`)
            THEN `the person lawfully administering my affairs`
        OTHERWISE `I do`

§§ `195AWA, 195AWB -- my written consent`

-- s 195AWA(2): "It is not an infringement of a moral right of an author in respect of a work to do, or omit to do, something
-- if the act or omission is within the scope of a written consent genuinely given by the author or a person representing the
-- author." (3): a consent "does not have any effect unless it is given: (a) in relation to specified acts or omissions, or
-- specified classes or types of acts or omissions ...; and (b) in relation to ... a specified work or specified works ... or
-- works of a particular description". (4): "A consent may be given by an employee for the benefit of his or her employer in
-- relation to all or any acts or omissions ... and in relation to all works made or to be made by the employee in the course
-- of his or her employment."
-- s 195AWB: the consent "does not have any effect" if duress was applied, or if a statement known to be "false or misleading
-- in a material particular" was made "with the intention of persuading the other person to give ... a consent".
-- Films and works in films come under s 195AW, not encoded.
DECLARE `My written consent` HAS
    `there is a consent` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you (or someone representing you) consented to the act or omission
    `it is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the consent is in writing
    `it was genuinely given` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it was genuinely given by you or a person representing you
    `I gave it as an employee for my employer, covering work in my employment` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether you gave it as an employee, for your employer's benefit, for works made in the course of your employment
    `it specifies the acts or classes of acts` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it names the acts or omissions, or classes or types of them, that it covers
    `it specifies the works or a description of works` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether it names the works, or describes works not yet made or being made, that it covers
    `the act is within its scope` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether what was done falls within what the consent covers
    `duress was applied to obtain it` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether duress was applied to you to get the consent
    `a knowingly false statement persuaded me` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether someone, knowing a statement was false or misleading in a material particular, made it to persuade you to consent
    `the work is a film or in a film` IS A BOOLEAN
    @desc Whether the work is a cinematograph film or included in one

DECLARE `Consent outcome` IS ONE OF
    `my consent covers it, so it does not infringe my moral rights`
    `my consent has no effect or does not reach it`
    `not answered here: films are under section 195AW`

@export Does my written consent stop this being an infringement of my moral rights (ss 195AWA, 195AWB)?
GIVEN `c` IS A `My written consent` @desc The facts about your consent
GIVETH A `Consent outcome`
DECIDE `Does my consent cover it` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `c`'s `the work is a film or in a film`
            THEN `not answered here: films are under section 195AW`
        IF `the consent has effect` `c` AND `c`'s `the act is within its scope`
            THEN `my consent covers it, so it does not infringe my moral rights`
        OTHERWISE `my consent has no effect or does not reach it`

GIVEN `c` IS A `My written consent`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consent has effect` IF
        `c`'s `there is a consent`
    AND `c`'s `it is in writing`
    AND `c`'s `it was genuinely given`
    AND (   `c`'s `I gave it as an employee for my employer, covering work in my employment`
         OR (`c`'s `it specifies the acts or classes of acts` AND `c`'s `it specifies the works or a description of works`))
    AND (NOT `c`'s `duress was applied to obtain it`)
    AND (NOT `c`'s `a knowingly false statement persuaded me`)

§§ `194(1), 195AO, 195AR, 195AX -- is my right of attribution infringed`

-- s 195AO: a person infringes the right of attribution "if the person does, or authorises the doing of, an attributable act in
-- respect of the work without the identification of the author in accordance with Division 2 as the author of the work".
-- s 194(1): for a literary work the attributable acts are "(a) to reproduce the work in a material form; (b) to publish the
-- work; (c) to perform the work in public; (d) to communicate the work to the public; (e) to make an adaptation of the work."
-- s 195AR(1): no infringement "if the person establishes that it was reasonable in all the circumstances not to identify the
-- author" -- a judgment for the court, so an INPUT. s 195AX: "It is not an infringement of an author's moral right in respect
-- of a work to do, or omit to do, something outside Australia." Rental and acts on an adaptation are not attributable acts.
-- Artistic works (s 194(2)) are left out.
@export Is my right to be named as author infringed when my code is shipped without my name (ss 194, 195AO, 195AR, 195AWA, 195AX)?
GIVEN `the work` IS A `My work` @desc The facts about the work
      `what` IS A `What is done` @desc What is done with it
      `I am identified as the author` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are identified as the author when it is done
      `it was reasonable in all the circumstances not to identify me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court would find it reasonable in all the circumstances not to name you (the nature, purpose, manner and context of use, industry practice)
      `my consent` IS A `My written consent` @desc Any written consent you gave
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my right of attribution infringed` IF
        `Do I have moral rights in it` `the work` TRUE TRUE
    AND (   `Is it a literary work` (`the work`'s `the kind`)
         OR `the work`'s `the kind` EQUALS `a dramatic work`
         OR `the work`'s `the kind` EQUALS `a musical work`)
    AND (CONSIDER `what`'s `the act`
         WHEN `reproduce it in a material form` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `publish it` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `perform it in public` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `communicate it to the public` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `make an adaptation of it` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND `what`'s `it is done or authorised in Australia`
    AND (NOT `I am identified as the author`)
    AND (NOT `it was reasonable in all the circumstances not to identify me`)
    AND (NOT (`Does my consent cover it` `my consent` EQUALS `my consent covers it, so it does not infringe my moral rights`))
